---
import Layout from "../layout/Layout.astro";
import siteMetaData from "../constants/siteMetaData.json";
---

<Layout seo={siteMetaData.pages.privacyPolicy} class="flex justify-center">
  <article class="privacy-policy max-w-300 px-5 py-15">
    <h1 class="relative mb-8 clamp-[text,1.4rem,2.25rem] font-semibold before:absolute before:bottom-0 before:clamp-[w,4rem,7rem] before:h-1 before:bg-lime-green">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-gray/75">
      Last updated: November 5, 2026. This page describes how this Thivi Edu
      portfolio demonstration handles information when you browse the site.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Information you enter</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form on this demonstration site is not connected to a
        server. When you submit it, the name and email fields are checked in
        your browser, a demonstration message is shown, and the form is reset.
        The information you enter is not sent to or stored by Thivi Edu through
        this form. Please do not enter sensitive personal information.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Google Maps and your preference</h2>
      <p>
        The embedded Google Map is optional. It is not loaded unless you choose
        “Allow Google Maps” and then select “Show map”. If you decline, the
        embedded map is not loaded; you can still choose to open Google Maps
        using the link on the Contact page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your choice is saved in this browser’s local storage under the key
        <code>thivi-google-maps-consent</code>, with a value of
        <code>accepted</code> or <code>rejected</code>. This is browser storage,
        not a cookie, and the choice is not sent to our site’s server. It stays
        in your browser until you change the map preference on the Contact page
        or clear this site’s browser data. If browser storage is unavailable,
        your choice may not persist after you leave the page.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you allow and load the map, your browser connects to Google. Google
        may receive technical information such as your IP address and browser
        details, and may use cookies or similar technologies according to its
        own policies. Declining prevents the embedded map from loading, but
        following the external Google Maps link will take you to Google and is
        subject to Google’s policies.
      </p>
      <p class="flex gap-1">
        For more information, see
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="underline underline-offset-4"
        >
          Google’s Privacy Policy
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This demonstration does not intentionally use analytics or advertising
        cookies. The map preference is stored in local storage as described
        above. Google Maps, if loaded, is a third-party service and may use its
        own cookies or similar technologies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
      <p class="flex gap-1">
        This notice may be updated if the site’s features change. If you have a
        question about this demonstration, contact us at
        <a
          href="mailto:contact@thivi.com.au"
          class="underline underline-offset-4"
        >
          contact@thivi.com.au
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-gray/75">
      This page describes the current behavior of a portfolio demonstration and
      is not legal advice. A live service should review this notice against its
      actual data practices and applicable requirements.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-policy > :global(section) {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .privacy-policy > :global(section h2) {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-dark-olive-green);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 1.5vw + 0.9rem, 1.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .privacy-policy > :global(section p:not(:last-child)) {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  code {
    padding-inline-start: 5px;
  }
</style>
